Kubernetes with K3s
What is K3s?
K3s is a lightweight Kubernetes distribution developed by Rancher Labs and certified by CNCF (Cloud Native Computing Foundation).
It contains all core Kubernetes features but consumes less CPU and memory compared to a standard Kubernetes installation.

Why K3s?

In production environments, companies use:

kubeadm clusters
Amazon EKS
Azure AKS
Google GKE
OpenShift

For learning purposes, K3s is preferred because:

Easy installation
Low resource consumption
Same Kubernetes APIs
Same kubectl commands
Same YAML manifests

Important: Everything you learn in K3s works exactly the same in EKS, AKS, GKE, and kubeadm clusters
