Components Explanation
API Server

The API Server is the brain of Kubernetes.

Whenever we run:
kubectl get pods, kubectl create deployment and kubectl delete pod

kubectl talks to the API Server.

The API Server receives all requests and coordinates cluster operations.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Scheduler

The Scheduler decides:

"On which node should this Pod run?"

If the cluster contains multiple worker nodes, Scheduler selects the best node based on available resources.
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Controller Manager

The Controller Manager continuously checks whether the cluster state matches the desired state.

Example:

Desired Pods = 3

Running Pods = 2

Controller Manager automatically creates one more Pod.
---------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Kubelet

Kubelet runs on every worker node.

Responsibilities:

Communicates with API Server
Creates Pods
Monitors Pod health
Restarts failed containers
Container Runtime

Container Runtime actually runs containers.

K3s uses:

containerd

Responsibilities:

Pull images
Create containers
Start containers
Stop containers
